{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"d73672952e1f1156c3f917d589d049f2bca0a39465f86c242d902a7053ba496f","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira reconciler inbound link diffing","key_entities":["inbound_differ.py","_diff_links_inbound","apply_inbound_records.py","_inbound_update_apply_links","rebar.unlink","binding_store","managed_refs","test_inbound_delete_link_round_trips","outbound_links.py","_diff_link_removals"],"problem_keywords":["inbound link deletion","asymmetric differ","add-only reconciliation","peer link removal not mirrored","local-wins semantics"],"propositions":["inbound_differ is ADD-only by construction and never mirrors link removals, while outbound_links has a removal path, creating asymmetry","a link deleted in Jira stays on the local rebar ticket forever because no pass evaluates its absence","apply_inbound_records silently discards non-add link records via action check, preventing any removal from reaching the store","the correct arbitration requires per-binding peer-state history (like 1296's parent template) to distinguish never-pushed local links from peer-deleted links, avoiding data loss","ecosystem research shows link deletion propagation is not commonly handled and carries data-loss risk; local-wins-and-restore is the deferred design, failing safe and identical to peer behavior"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787776281849842001,"uuid":"32452fc8-3744-4452-a461-000a5348a5b2"}